  "basis": "The chart's vertical scale is inverted, with the value 0 at the top and 35 at the bottom. The task asks for the 'highest per-barrel cost'. On this scale, the highest cost corresponds to the largest numerical value, which is located at the lowest vertical position on the page. The 1980 data point is the lowest on the chart, positioned below the '35' tick mark (indicating a value > 35). The 1976 and 1986 data points are near the top of the chart, between the '10' and '15' ticks (indicating values between 10 and 15). Therefore, 1980 represents the highest cost.",
